Z||000000||batboy||03-14-2000||03:51 PM||||THE 50 STEPS OF A BATBOY FIERO PROJECT<P>1. Daydreaming about modifying your Fiero's Gee-Whiz<BR>2. Surf the web late at night for several week researching<BR>3. Find three ways to modify the Gee-Whiz<BR>4. Cross out one way to modify it as being retarded<BR>5. Ask the Fiero Forum if anyone has modified their Gee-Whiz<BR>6. A half dozen respond and discuss everything but the Gee-Whiz<BR>7. Post another question about the Fiero Gee-Whiz mod<BR>8. After much discussion, it is decided which method is best<BR>9. Turns out the retarded method you crossed out is the best<BR>10. Figure out a list of items needed for the Gee-Whiz mod<BR>11. Spend several days to find out nothing is available locally<BR>12. Ask the Forum if the parts are available on-line<BR>13. After much discussion, it is decided the parts are around<BR>14. Check credit card spending limit and bank account<BR>15. Call credit card company to increase spending limit<BR>16. Find enough cash in bank for next minimum card payment<BR>17. Order six different parts from five different places<BR>18. One guy calls back and says, "Sorry dude, out of stock!"<BR>19. Ask the Forum if anyone knows a different place to find it<BR>20. After much discussion, a member finds out he has an extra<BR>21. Emails are exchanged and part is shipped for only postage<BR>22. Parts begin arriving via post office and UPS truck<BR>23. One part don't quite fit, two hours are spend sanding it<BR>24. After much discussion on the Forum, cheaper parts are found<BR>25. Cuss myself for paying more than I had to<BR>26. Look at all the parts to modify the Fiero's Gee-Whiz<BR>27. Gather up all the tools needed to do the job<BR>28. Discover you don't have one of the needed tools<BR>29. Drive to Sears and buy the appropriate Craftsman tool<BR>30. Dismantle stuff in order to access the Gee-Whizz<BR>31. Break one of those little Doo-Hickies that holds it in<BR>32. Ask the Forum if those Doo-Hickies are still available<BR>33. After much discussion, the Doo-Hickies are no longer made<BR>34. Ogre tells how to modify a Thingie-Jiggie into a Doo-Hickie<BR>35. Ask the Forum if those Thingie-Jiggies are still available<BR>36. After much discussion, someone's cousin's brother has one<BR>37. Weeks later a well used Thingie-Jiggie arrives in the mail<BR>38. The Thingie-Jiggie is modified into a Doo-Hickie<BR>39. The Gee-Whiz is modified and reinstalled, but a bolt breaks<BR>40. Half an afternoon wasted drilling out the broken bolt<BR>41. A dozen coffee cans full of old bolts and not one that fits<BR>42. Drive to the hardware store for a new bolt<BR>43. At home again, find out you got the wrong size<BR>44. Back to the hardware store to get the right size bolt<BR>45. After putting a bandaid onto a knuckle, admire handiwork<BR>46. Take Fiero for test drive, Gee-Whiz mod works!<BR>47. Brag about how easy to do the mod on the Fiero Forum<BR>48. After much discussion, several members ask for pics<BR>49. Take a bunch of digital pics and spend hours posting them<BR>50. Start daydreaming about your next Fiero project...<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-14-2000).]||||reg||10
